    "body": "### Problem\n\nI'm having a strange issue where sometimes, when I press a key (or a sequence of keys), I see what I have pressed in my status bar, but the corresponding action does not happen until I press another key or wait a few (3-5) seconds.\nI have no idea if the actions \"happened on the computer\" but the screen/TUI hasn't updated yet, or if nvim is actually waiting for me to do something, similar to timeouts when you have two keymaps with the same prefix.\n\nExample:\n- i press `dd` to delete a line\n- i see `dd` in the bottom right of my statusbar\n- nothing happens for a few seconds, then the line is deleted\n\nThis is really hard to capture on camera as it happens unpredictably.\nIf I ever get the chance I will post a video here.\n\n### Things i've already tried:\n- Changing the `timeoutlen`\n- Tried `foot`, `kitty`, `alacritty` terminals. It happens less often on `kitty`\n- Other nvim versions: v0.13.0-nightly\n- `nvim --clean`, so it can't be a plugin or misconfigured keymaps\n\n### Things i haven't tried (yet):\n- Another Window manager; maybe sway has some strange refresh mechanisms that don't work properly?\n- Disabling Intel PSR (from what i know, it should not cause delayed screen updates but you never know)\n- External monitor\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\nnvim --clean\n:edit foo\n# edit the file normally as you would...\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe actions happen instantly.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.5, happens on nightly too\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nhaven't noticed anything yet, vim 9.2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora 44 Sway (Linux 7.2.9-200.fc44.x86_64)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot, kitty, alacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nfoot, xterm-kitty, alacritty\n\n### Installation\n\ndnf for 0.12.5, build for nightly\n\n### System information\nThinkPad X9 15p with X7 358H CPU",
